os_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Elasticsearch Version\n\n8.18.3\n\n### Installed Plugins\n\n_No response_\n\n### Java Version\n\n_bundled_\n\n### OS Version\n\nChainguard 5.15.0-1086-azure (Elastic Cloud)\n\n### Problem Description\n\nIt is possible to update a running transform by posting to its `_update` API. \n\n[Docs](https://www.elastic.co/docs/api/doc/elasticsearch/operation/operation-transform-update-transform) say:\n> All updated properties except description do not take effect until after the transform starts the next checkpoint, thus there is data consistency in each checkpoint.\n\nHowever - we have found that updating the `frequency` parameter does not take effect until the transform is stopped and restarted. \n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\nEnable trace logging for `TransformTask`:\n\n```\nPUT _cluster/settings\n{\n  \"transient\": {\n    \"logger.org.elasticsearch.xpack.transform.transforms.TransformTask\": \"TRACE\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- Define a transform with `frequency: 1m`\n- Start the transform\n- Observe trigger pattern in logs (some log message with format `\"[%s] triggered(event=%s) \"`)\n- Post an update to the transform to reduce frequency to 1 second. \n- Note no change to triggering behaviour in logs.\n\n### Logs (if relevant)\n\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"prwhelan","id":1223797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjM3OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1223797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prwhelan","html_url":"https://github.com/p